= Genoa Conference

An international economic conference is held to address major economic and political issues revolving around europe and to address the status of **<span style="color: #000;">Ge</span><span style="color: #D00;">rma</span><span style="color: #FC0;">ny</span>** and the **<span style="color: #CD0000;">Soviet Union</span>**, both of which have been excluded from the **<span style="color: #000091;">Pa</span><span style="color: #CCC;">r</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">is</span>** Conference in 1919.

The conference was also held to negotiate and build a relationship between **<span style="color: #000091;">West</span><span style="color: #CCC;">ern Eu</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">rope</span>** and **<span style="color: #FFB81C;">East</span><span style="color: #046A38;">ern Eu</span><span style="color: #BE3A34;">rope</span>**.

**<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">and</span>** is represented through it's formal delegates led by its Foreign Minister, [+ foreign_minister +].

- @border

@border
title: Polish eastern border question
  
The **<span style="color: #000091;">West</span><span style="color: #CCC;">ern Po</span><span style="color: #E1000F;">wers</span>** have initiated a discussion regarding the legitimacy of the <span class="wide_tooltip-wrap">Treaty of Riga<span class="wide_tooltip-tip">The treaty that ended the Polish-Soviet war and drew the Polish-Soviet border, not recognized by the Western Powers.</span></span>.

The **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** delegates argued for the legitimacy of the Eastern Borders. additionally to further solidify their position, the **<span style="color: #CCC;">Pol</span><span style="color: #DC143C;">ish</span>** delegates discussed with the **<span  style="color: #CD0000;">Soviet</span>** delegates offering to recognize the Bolshevik government in exchange for them to recognize the treaty and the border.

